<title>USA: Murphy Oil sees $17.7 mln gain from sale.</title>
<headline>Murphy Oil sees $17.7 mln gain from sale.</headline>
<dateline>EL DORADO, Ark 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Murphy Oil Corp said Monday its sale of 48 onshore oil and gas fields in the United States should result in an after-tax gain of about $17.7 million in the third quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Company President and Chief Executive Claiborne Deming said the company would deploy the proceeds of the $47 million sale in &quot;high-return oil and gas projects&quot; under development in the Gulf of Mexico. Those projects are expected to come on stream in late 1996 or early 1997.</p>
<p>The fields sold were primarily in Alabama, Arkansas, Louisiana, Mississippi and Texas.</p>
